{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1232817-using-beasts-as-antagonists","id":1232817,"title":"Using Beasts as antagonists","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-06T00:59:13-07:00","id":1232817,"title":"Using Beasts as antagonists","content":"For a one shot chronicle I'm looking for a boogey man type of antagonist and I was thinking why not a Begotten? Any tips or thoguhts about that? The theme of the game could be &quot;Growing Up Sucks&quot; with a bunch of teents discovering about the uglier truth of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T04:51:24-07:00","id":1232832,"title":"","content":"Are the players high school students? <br /> What about a Talassi with Hunger for Punishment? <br /> In the school people starts to vanish, the players investigates and discovers all the dirty secrets of the kidnapped people. <br /> In the end a nerd, meek and loner, is the Beast keeping the bullies captive for punishment in his Lair Chamber modeled on the school basement. <br /> The player could also decide in the end that the Beast is the &quot;good guy&quot;of the story...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T04:55:16-07:00","id":1232833,"title":"","content":"They work pretty easy as it, I've done it before though I've used the Inheritances, which are more physically monstrous. They have a lot of powers you can use to hit the entire PC group but not necessarily kill them all in one hit the way a high-specc'd combat person could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T07:54:10-07:00","id":1232861,"title":"","content":"Beasts are great as one-shot antagonists, or even longer term ones. A Predator makes an easy Serial Killer. A Collector, a thief or abductor. A Tyrant could as easily lord over an office.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T10:24:31-07:00","id":1232876,"title":"","content":"Maybe have the players try to enter the world of part time jobs and their boss turns out to be a Talassi Tyrant?<br /> <br /> Their lair could take the form of a dungeon, with the employees forced to perform slave labor under grueling conditions?<br /> <br /> As they toil away in the master's dungeon, they are slowly drained of any hope of freedom or creativity, until they eventually become a mindless, corporate drone who simply takes orders and doesn't ask questions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-06T10:52:43-07:00","id":1232884,"title":"","content":"I think answering the question of <i>how</i> growing up sucks will go a long way in deciding which Beast you have, with, hell, that being the point of the lesson. And from there, it's probably easiest to see the answer to that when you look at the lies the characters really believe.<br /> <br /> So, you know. What are the character's delusions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T01:47:19-07:00","id":1233015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1232817-using-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1232884#post1232884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think answering the question of <i>how</i> growing up sucks will go a long way in deciding which Beast you have, with, hell, that being the point of the lesson. And from there, it's probably easiest to see the answer to that when you look at the lies the characters really believe.<br /> <br /> So, you know. What are the character's delusions?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as they developed their concepts we have two overtly opmistic guys and a nice guy that acts in a far harsher manner than he is. We could say that they believe the world is a safe place and adults can be trusted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T03:52:28-07:00","id":1233027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>damocles23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1232817-using-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1233015#post1233015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as they developed their concepts we have two overtly opmistic guys and a nice guy that acts in a far harsher manner than he is. We could say that they believe the world is a safe place and adults can be trusted.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Ravager is likely smacking their lips after hearing that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T03:55:47-07:00","id":1233028,"title":"","content":"Ravager (to destroy that sense of safety) or Tempter (to corrupt that trust in adults), I am thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T15:07:16-07:00","id":1233093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1232817-using-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1233028#post1233028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ravager (to destroy that sense of safety) or Tempter (to corrupt that trust in adults), I am thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean an Enabler?<br /> <br /> My takes would be Ravager, Tyrant, and Nemesis, depending on the particular nature of that trust in adults(and hell, why not all three, have a little brood), but I think the most insidious form would be a Tyrant-the adults have power <i>because they take it from you</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T15:12:46-07:00","id":1233095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1232817-using-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1233093#post1233093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean an Enabler?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I knew it wasn't Tempter (that's a Demon categorization), but my mind blanked on what it actually was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1232817-using-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1233093#post1233093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My takes would be Ravager, Tyrant, and Nemesis, depending on the particular nature of that trust in adults(and hell, why not all three, have a little brood), but I think the most insidious form would be a Tyrant-the adults have power <i>because they take it from you</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would also fit into &quot;Growing up sucks&quot; in that it (usually) means you have to work, which for most means working <i>for</i> someone, and thus under their power (to a greater or lesser extent).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T15:17:01-07:00","id":1233096,"title":"","content":"Do you plan on the monsters truly being evil or trying to teach a lesson, even if your characters don't see it that way? Either way works, though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T22:27:42-07:00","id":1233143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1232817-using-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1233096#post1233096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you plan on the monsters truly being evil or trying to teach a lesson, even if your characters don't see it that way? Either way works, though</div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhat ambiguos. The Beast in question may think they are giving a lesson but their methods are downright cruel. It's the kind of Beast that would not see themselves as evil but everyone would disagree. Even other Beasts may think &quot;this guy is cray cray&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-07T22:40:06-07:00","id":1233145,"title":"","content":"All three of them? Not the downright cruel part, but the &quot;this guy is Cray Cray&quot; part. Just wondering because so far, unless I'm misinterpreting it, all three beast are of a different family and or hunger, you sure not one of them could possibly be the &quot;only sane man&quot; among them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T03:11:32-07:00","id":1233159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1232817-using-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1233145#post1233145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All three of them? Not the downright cruel part, but the &quot;this guy is Cray Cray&quot; part. Just wondering because so far, unless I'm misinterpreting it, all three beast are of a different family and or hunger, you sure not one of them could possibly be the &quot;only sane man&quot; among them?</div> </div> </div> </div>It culd be but I'm planning on having only one Beast, though. Since my players want to do a one shot and don't know anything about CofD I'd like to play up the inscrutable and creepy side of Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T09:45:17-07:00","id":1233214,"title":"","content":"Oh ok I understand now. Good luck on the one shot (and make their horrors scary as hell!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T10:05:48-07:00","id":1233216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1232817-using-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1233214#post1233214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh ok I understand now. Good luck on the one shot (and make their horrors scary as hell!)</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. Remember, Horrors are <i>literally</i> myths of fear. That should come across. Make 'em <i> mean.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T10:19:26-07:00","id":1233217,"title":"","content":"Also, while I'm fairly certain that you can't make a horror titanic or tiny in size, don't be afraid to really make the horror really big and imposing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T10:35:03-07:00","id":1233218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1232817-using-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1233217#post1233217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, while I'm fairly certain that you can't make a horror titanic or tiny in size, don't be afraid to really make the horror really big and imposing</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the piece the resistance should be the moment they do enter the lair of the beast haunting the school (Either a Talassi or an Eshmaki but <i>definitely </i>a Tyrant) and then the Horror shows up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-08T21:58:10-07:00","id":1233348,"title":"","content":"So, I love this idea, and others have made some really great points! Here's something I thought of that nobody's mentioned:<br /> <br /> Why not have a Hero show up at some point? You said the theme here is &quot;growning up sucks.&quot; Another nice way to highlight that is the idea that &quot;you're just pawns in someone else's game.&quot; At the same time your Tyrant Beast is tightening its grip on the players, or your Ravager is pulling their world down around them, you could have a Hero show up to save them...and <i>then </i>try to sacrifice them in the name of &quot;the Greater Good.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T03:53:54-07:00","id":1233379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1232817-using-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1233348#post1233348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I love this idea, and others have made some really great points! Here's something I thought of that nobody's mentioned:<br /> <br /> Why not have a Hero show up at some point? You said the theme here is &quot;growning up sucks.&quot; Another nice way to highlight that is the idea that &quot;you're just pawns in someone else's game.&quot; At the same time your Tyrant Beast is tightening its grip on the players, or your Ravager is pulling their world down around them, you could have a Hero show up to save them...and <i>then </i>try to sacrifice them in the name of &quot;the Greater Good.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to marry this idea. Maybe, he could be an older friend or even a relative. Plot twist!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T06:09:47-07:00","id":1233396,"title":"","content":"One thing I just realized. As much as I love that movie the Horror as I envisioned it looks too much like IT. What would be another cool motif?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T06:16:34-07:00","id":1233400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>damocles23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1232817-using-beasts-as-antagonists?p=1233396#post1233396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I just realized. As much as I love that movie the Horror as I envisioned it looks too much like IT. What would be another cool motif?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Dragon, from Evgeny Schwartz' <i>The Dragon</i> could serve as inspiration? Just read the quote here:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evgeny_Schwartz#The_Dragon\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e9/Evgeny_Shvarts_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evgeny_Schwartz#The_Dragon\" target=\"_blank\"> Evgeny Schwartz - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evgeny_Schwartz#The_Dragon\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evgeny_Schwartz#The_Dragon </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T22:43:33-07:00","id":1233618,"title":"","content":"So, I think I have figured out an outline of the story.<br /> We'll start in a small town of California (If any of you are from there, we apologize. We know you don't abide man eating monsters. We hope.) with the characters being first year highschoolers. There is a distinct creepy mood in the town, that &quot;I'm ok, you're ok, everyone is ok&quot; kind of mindset...Just as countless drifters, vagrants and problem kids are disappearing, including some from the main character's families. They are a tight knit group of friends that will probaly start investigating once they see that the Beast (Choosing the family is becoming more and more complicated because she fits is so many!) is very proactive with her Nightmares. That and a mixture of complacency because people know that there is something wrong with the twon, it's in their skin, but if it doesn't involve them they don't care. &quot;First they came for the Socialists...&quot; and all that. We'll introduce several possible Red Herrings, teachers, parents and that creepy drifter who has definitely killed someone (who'll later be revealed as the Hero) only to find out that the Dragon, that's how she calls herself is one of their classmates. Possibly the Goth Girl because my players expect one but they don't expect her to be villain. All of this will culminate at the Beast's hideout/Lair, an old construction site with plenty of natural and supernatural hazard where they will attempt to slay the Dragon...Or die trying.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T06:39:39-07:00","id":1233679,"title":"","content":"What about a sort of reversal of the theme &quot;the princess and the dragon&quot;? <br /> The goth girl could be a gothic lolita with the obsession of being cute and kawaii, because in the deep she feels ugly and monstrous (maybe someone bullied her on her appearance). <br /> Her lair could be a sort of &quot;towers &quot; where she keep a &quot;court&quot; made of the prisoners, playing whit her &quot;dolls&quot; in a sort of wicked game to gain gifts, attention and affection (with intimidation and punishments)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T06:49:28-07:00","id":1233683,"title":"","content":"A Namtaru Tyrant, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3997-damocles23","name":"damocles23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T07:00:42-07:00","id":1233689,"title":"","content":"Or a collector","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}